            <ArticleTitle>Cryosurgery for chronic injuries of the cutaneous nerve in the upper limb. Analysis of a new open technique.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>413-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We have treated six patients with chronic pain following nerve injury using a cryosurgical probe. All had a significant return of hand function and improvement of pain during a mean follow-up of 13.5 months. Open visualisation of the injured nervous tissue is essential for patients undergoing this technique. Four patients regained normal sensation in the dermatome of the previously injured nerve.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
